		{"id":"0ac40b930b03cb6a","type":"text","text":"## Standard Deviation\n\nMeasure of how spread out numbers are\n\n* Its symbol is **σ** (the greek letter sigma)\n* Formula is the square root of the **variance**\n\n#### Variance\n\nThe average of the squared differences from the mean.\n\n* Calculate the mean\n* for each number subtract the mean and square the result (squared difference)\n* Calculate the average of those squared difference","x":-180,"y":-120,"width":520,"height":320},
		{"id":"8b0c0f9848af4c43","type":"file","file":"Attachments/Pasted image 20261113115430.png","x":380,"y":-626,"width":400,"height":212},
		{"id":"31873697ee469376","type":"text","text":"# Anomaly review metrics — worked example\n\n  \n\nReference for interpreting the fact-data **Delta deviation** findings on the Portal anomaly review page.\n\n  \n\n## What we are measuring\n\n  \n\nFor **one slice** (account, entity, scenario, and other non-time dimensions), the engine uses **period-to-period changes**:\n\n  \n\n**Change (delta)** = this period’s amount − last period’s amount\n\n  \n\nAll four metric tiles refer to those **changes**, not the raw balance level on the chart alone.\n\n  \n\n### Prior period change\n\n  \n\nThe change for the **flagged period only** (this period minus last).\n\n  \n\n### Average period change\n\n\nThe **usual** change each period — the mean of historical period-to-period changes for this slice.\n\nAnswers: *What step does this slice usually take?*\n\n### Delta variation\n\n\n**Standard deviation** of those changes — how much they typically spread around the average (choppiness).\n\nAnswers: *How noisy are those steps?* (a different question from the average.)\n\n  \n\n### Delta z-score\n\n  \n\nHow many “spreads” this period’s change is from the average change.\n\n\n---\n\n## Example numbers (from the UI)\n\n  \n\n- **Prior period change:** −728.68\n\n- **Average period change:** −31.68\n\n- **Delta variation:** 148.60\n\n- **Delta z-score:** 4.7\n\n  \n\n**Chart story:** Amounts are flat for many periods, then a sharp drop at **2025 P12** (highlighted point).\n\n  \n\n---\n\n## Z-score\n  \n\nz = (prior period change − average period change) ÷ delta variation\n  \n\nWith this finding:\n  \n\n- z = (−728.68 − (−31.68)) ÷ 148.60\n\n- z = −697 ÷ 148.60\n\n- z ≈ −4.7\n\n  \n\nThe UI may show **4.7** without the minus sign; the move is **below** the average change.\n\n  \n\n**Plain language:** This period’s change is about **4.7 typical spreads below** the average period change.\n\n  \n\n**Rearranged:**\n\n  \n\nprior period change ≈ average period change + (z × delta variation)\n\n  \n\n−728.68 ≈ −31.68 + (−4.7 × 148.6)\n\n  \n\n---\n\n  \n\n## Why 148.6 × 4.7 is not 729\n\n  \n\n- **728.68** is the full **prior period change** (total drop vs last period).\n\n- **697** is the **surprise**: prior change − average change, which is −728.68 − (−31.68).\n\n- **148.6 × 4.7 ≈ 698** is the same surprise: **z × delta variation**.\n\n- **31.68 + 697 ≈ 729** is the usual step plus the surprise, which equals the total move.\n\n  \n\n**z × spread** is the distance **from the average change**, not the full prior change, unless you add the average back in.\n\n  \n\n---\n\n  \n\n## Normal distribution (rule of thumb)\n\n  \n\nIf period changes were roughly bell-shaped around the average:\n\n  \n\n- About **68%** fall within **±1** delta variation of the average\n\n- About **95%** fall within **±2**\n\n- About **99.7%** fall within **±3**\n\n  \n\nIllustrative band for this slice (average −31.68, spread 148.6):\n\n  \n\n−31.68 ± 148.6 → roughly **−180 to +117**\n\n  \n\nA change of **−728** is far outside that band, which matches **|z| ≈ 4.7**. The engine flags when **|z|** exceeds the configured threshold (minimum **3**).\n\n  \n\nReal data are not always normally distributed; the engine still uses this standardized distance.\n\n  \n\n---\n\n  \n\n## Stakeholder one-liner\n\n  \n\nAt **2025 P12** this slice fell about **729** more than the prior period. It usually moves about **32** down per period, with typical wiggle about **149**. This drop was about **4.7** of those wiggles **below** the usual step, so it was flagged.\n\n  \n\n---\n\n  \n\n## How Delta deviation fits together\n\n  \n\n1. Build period-to-period deltas for each slice.\n\n2. Compute **average period change** and **delta variation** (std dev of those deltas).\n\n3. Compute **z** = (this period’s delta − average) ÷ variation (leave-one-out stats when enough history exists).\n\n4. Flag when **|z|** is above threshold.\n\n  \n\n**Delta variation** is the standard deviation of **changes**, not of the **amounts** plotted on the time-series chart.","x":-1000,"y":-359,"width":2680,"height":1319},
		{"id":"da72932eb6abac40","type":"text","text":"“**P12** dropped **729** **more** than the **prior period**; this slice **usually** moves about **−32** per period, with **typical wiggle about ±149**. That **drop** is about **4.7** of those **wiggles** **below** the **usual** step — why it’s flagged.”","x":-460,"y":-680,"width":540,"height":160}
	],
